  "body": "Stacked on #3353. Merge #3353 first.\n\n## What changed\n\nFace shows the shared \"Pass starts at\" row on its Passes tab. The disabled combo shows Auto. The visible reason says that Face rows run edge to edge, so there is no inside or outside order.\n\n- `pass_start_row.rs` supplies the disabled row and its reason. `mill2d_page.rs` draws it on the Face Passes tab.\n- MCP refuses every `pass_start` value on Face, including `auto`. The message names the row order. The command does not change the job.\n- The Face guide records the disabled row. `docs/decisions/3356-face-pass-start.md` records the choice and this review repair.\n\nThe issue permits this result: \"If Face has no pass order, its row says so by name, and the issue records why.\"\n\n## Review repair\n\nThe stack includes corrected parent `9939a6238`. Inside and Outside use level curves from one side, clipped into open pieces. This replaces the whole-loop rank that cut full-width slots after a band split. Auto keeps its existing planner.\n\nThe parent's new pins measure engagement along the whole level. The hint, guide, decision, and MCP skill state where full-width cuts can still occur. The toolpath reports those cases with a warning.\n\nThe branch also includes upstream main `68d645261`. This revision contains the post dialog overlap fix for the checkbox failure reported by the review.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nThe merging session owns the process version bump.\n\n## Tests\n\nMutation checks passed. Disabling the corrected ring planner makes the split-band pin fail: 8.000 mm cut width exceeds the 5.150 mm bound. Restoring the planner makes it pass. Removing the post dialog scrollbar gutter reproduces the reviewed checkbox failure. Restoring the gutter makes the checkbox pin pass.\n\nGate results include `pass_start_levels` (5 passed), `face_pass_start` (1 passed), and `offset_pass_start` (3 passed, 2 ignored).\n\nRelevant pins:\n\n- `face_pass_start::mcp_refuses_pass_start_on_face_by_the_row_order`: all three values are refused with the Face reason, and the job stays unchanged.\n- `egui_app::tests::pass_start::the_face_passes_tab_says_it_has_no_pass_order`: the row, disabled Auto combo, and visible reason.\n- `pass_start_levels::outside_band_split_by_the_part_cuts_no_move_at_full_width`: engagement, overcut, and leftover along the whole reviewed split band.\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_outside_offset_cuts_no_move_at_full_width`: the inherited heavy pin checks both flanks along each whole fig8 level. It remains ignored in this debug gate and was not rerun during this repair.\n- `egui_app::post_dialog_tests::desktop_post_command_opens_dialog_and_applies_declared_script_options_undoably`: the post dialog option changes.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on `e44df8e2876c428c2a15711677489d247e3986e7`. The geometry change selected the batch fallback: 1,090 steps, 0 failures, 46.9 minutes. Used `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` and `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`. The first attempt hit stale seeded build artifacts. A clean worktree target rebuild cleared the errors..\nClippy on touched crates: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed as the final gate step..\nUI library suite on the final merge: 1,432 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored, with 6 parallel threads. The run took 66.43 seconds. No SIGSEGV occurred. The post dialog checkbox pin passed. UI integration suites also passed..\nThe full heavy gate was not rerun during this repair. The PR stays a draft. A reached heavy lane must pass before the PR is ready.\n\n## Face Passes views\n\nBefore: the Face Passes tab has no \"Pass starts at\" row.\n\n![Face Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/7bc8753d7/pr-3387/face-before.png)\n\nAfter: the disabled Auto combo and its reason are visible.\n\n![Face Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/7bc8753d7/pr-3387/face-after.png)\n\nScreenshots are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n## Goldens and limits\n\nFace output does not change. No golden or snapshot PNG changes are included.\n\nA project file with an unknown `pass_start` key on Face is not tested. Face writes no such key.\n\nChangelog: Face: the Passes tab shows \"Pass starts at\" as not used, with the reason (Face rows run edge to edge); MCP refuses pass_start on a Face by that reason.\n\nFixes #3356\n",
